{
 "about": "# Load-test knee of POST /resolve with the fake LLM. Holds the machine, the exact commands and one summary row per run (output of loadtest/resolve.py). Read by docs/RUNBOOK.md, docs/scale_out.md and loadtest/README.md; every number they quote comes from this file.",
 "date_utc": "2026-11-14",
 "machine": {
  "cpu": "Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-14450HX",
  "logical_cores": 16,
  "ram_gb": 22.6,
  "os": "Linux 7.0.0-43-generic",
  "python": "3.11.18",
  "ledger_disk": "NVMe SSD, ext4 (data/ on the root filesystem); the tmpfs series used /tmp (RAM)",
  "server_process": "one uvicorn worker (one event loop), load generator on the same machine"
 },
 "commands": {
  "server": "LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY= LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY= RESOLV_ENV=dev RESOLV_FAKE_LLM=1 FAKE_LLM_LATENCY_S=0.8 TRUSTED_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=X-Loadtest-IP ORDER_PROOF_SECRET=loadtest-secret RESOLV_DB=data/<dir>/resolv.db RESOLV_PSP_DB=data/<dir>/psp.db RESOLV_TELEMETRY=data/<dir>/live.jsonl uvicorn resolv.api.main:app --port 8020 --log-level warning",
  "proof": "ORDER_PROOF_SECRET=loadtest-secret python -c \"from resolv.api.auth import order_proof; print(order_proof('ORD-1187'))\"",
  "warm_up": "one 15 s run at --rate 2 after each server start (first requests pay lazy imports); not recorded",
  "load": "python -m loadtest.resolve --base http://localhost:8020 --order ORD-1187 --proof <code> --rate <r> --duration 60 --concurrency 400 --ip-header X-Loadtest-IP --fake-llm --out <dir>/rate<r>",
  "profile": "py-spy record --idle --format raw -- uvicorn ... (same server), 30 s at --rate 40, code 84c5c69"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Each /resolve makes two fake LLM calls of 0.8 s, so an unloaded request takes about 1.62 s.",
  "Langfuse keys are blanked so no traces leave the machine and tracing cost is not measured.",
  "Knee rule: the first rate where ok_per_s falls below 95% of the offered rate, /resolve p95 passes 2x its unloaded value, or /health p95 passes 100 ms.",
  "code 84c5c69 = before the fix (step journal and trail reads run sync SQLite on the event loop); code 1c0831f = after (those calls run in asyncio.to_thread)."
 ],
 "profile_before_fix_rate40": {
  "event_loop_samples": 3484,
  "idle_waiting_for_io_pct": 60.5,
  "inside_resolv_harness_ledger_pct": {
   "add_step (step journal commit)": 17.6,
   "tx (BEGIN/COMMIT)": 16.8,
   "connect (open + PRAGMAs)": 9.1,
   "audit.read": 4.7,
   "ledger.steps": 1.9
  },
  "reading": "About two thirds of the loop's busy time was sync SQLite; the commit fsync blocks every other request."
 },
